6-04-01T21:43:28Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:25:53Z","closed_at":"2026-04-07T23:25:53Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.6 custom build during HDR output dev\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8108) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 63.74 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn extremely rare cases the brightness of an Godot window with HDR output will flicker bright and then back to normal at a frequency of about once per two seconds or so. This seemed to happen when the Windows SDR Content Brightness slider was set to its minimum (80 nits reference white luminance). Simply adjusting the SDR content brightness slider resolved the issue immediately, even when it was set back to its original minimum setting. This lead me to believe that the issue is a windows bug and not related to Godot.\n\nI noticed this during development of the HDR output feature, but never mentioned it because it seemed extremely rare and because it appeared to be a bug in Windows (likely to do with the `SDRWhiteLevel` that Godot retrieves). I haven't seen the issue recently, so it's possible that the issue has been resolved due to the way that the `SDRWhiteLevel` is no not set if the request to retrieve it fails. Unfortunately, the state of the code relating to `SDRWhiteLevel` when I reproduced this bug.\n\n...But if anyone ever notices this sort of behaviour of Godot where the editor or game window appears to flicker to a different brightness or appear a different brightness than the rest of Windows, please post here so it can be tracked.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the Godot editor (or a game) with Window/request_hdr_output on using a screen and project that supports HDR otuput.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118092/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118092/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}